          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.224,
            0.238,
            0.242
          ],
          "content": "**Figure it Out**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.251,
            0.16,
            0.269
          ],
          "content": "**Q.1.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.283,
            0.424,
            0.334
          ],
          "content": "**Rihan marked a point on a piece of paper. How many lines can he draw that pass through the point?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.468,
            0.287,
            0.765,
            0.354
          ],
          "content": "**Sheetal marked two points on a piece of paper. How many different lines can she draw that pass through both of the points?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.37,
            0.572,
            0.388
          ],
          "content": "**Can you help Rihan and Sheetal find their answers?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.398,
            0.794,
            0.442
          ],
          "content": "Ans. Rihan can draw many/uncountable number of lines through the given point. Sheetal can draw only one line through the two given points."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.451,
            0.88,
            0.487
          ],
          "content": "**Q.2. Name the line segments in Fig. 2.4. Which of the five marked points are on exactly one of the line segments? Which are on two of the line segments?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.49,
            0.33,
            0.514
          ],
          "content": "Ans. $\\mathbf { L } \\overline { { \\mathbf { M } } } , \\overline { { \\mathbf { M } } } \\overline { { \\mathbf { P } } } , \\overline { { \\mathbf { P } } } \\overline { { \\mathbf { Q } } } , \\overline { { \\mathbf { Q } } } \\overline { { \\mathbf { R } } }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.524,
            0.881,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": "Points L and R are exactly on one line segment. Points M, P and Q are on two line segments."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.568,
            0.825,
            0.599
          ],
          "content": "**Q.3. Name the rays shown in Fig. 2.5. Is T the starting point of each of these rays?** $\\begin{array} { r l } { \\rightarrow \\rightarrow \\rightarrow } & { { } \\rightarrow } \\end{array}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.595,
            0.357,
            0.612
          ],
          "content": "Ans. TA, TB, TN and NB"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.623,
            0.668,
            0.641
          ],
          "content": "No, T is the starting point of TB, TN and TA but not of NB."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.65,
            0.881,
            0.685
          ],
          "content": "**Q.4. Draw a rough figure and write labels appropriately to illustrate each of the following:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.695,
            0.388,
            0.712
          ],
          "content": "**a. OP and OQ meet at O.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.722,
            0.472,
            0.74
          ],
          "content": "**b. XY and PQ intersect at point M.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.749,
            0.589,
            0.767
          ],
          "content": "**c. Line l contains points E and F but not point D.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.776,
            0.354,
            0.794
          ],
          "content": "**d. Point P lies on AB.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
